**`src/agents/tier1/memory-agent.ts` — TTL cleanup is O(n) with no time index**

The periodic cleanup (every 5 minutes) scans all entries. As the store grows, cleanup time grows linearly and can block the event loop briefly.

```typescript
// AFTER — maintain a min-heap (or sorted map) by expiry
import { Heap } from 'heap-js'; // or use a simple sorted array for small datasets

class VectorStore {
  private expiryQueue: Array<{ id: string; expiresAt: number }> = [];

  async store(entry: MemoryEntry): Promise<void> {
    this.entries.set(entry.id, entry);
    if (entry.embedding) this.embeddings.set(entry.id, entry.embedding);
    if (entry.ttl) {
      this.expiryQueue.push({ id: entry.id, expiresAt: entry.createdAt.getTime() + entry.ttl });
      this.expiryQueue.sort((a, b) => a.expiresAt - b.expiresAt); // or use a proper min-heap
    }
  }

  async cleanup(): Promise<number> {
    const now = Date.now();
    let cleaned = 0;
    // Only scan until we hit a non-expired entry
    while (this.expiryQueue.length > 0 && this.expiryQueue[0].expiresAt <= now) {
      const { id } = this.expiryQueue.shift()!;
      await this.delete(id);
      cleaned++;
    }
    return cleaned;
  }
}
```

**`src/agents/tier2/simulation-agent.ts` — plain `Map` cache with no size bound (confirmed)**

As noted above, replace with `LRUCache`. Without eviction, a long-lived `SimulationAgent` instance accumulates every unique scenario it ever ran.

**`src/agents/tier3/mutation-agent.ts` — `Math.random()` in `mutateHook` produces unbounded lineage trees**

Not a direct leak, but if `LineageNode` trees are stored in memory without a depth cap, deep evolutionary runs create large object graphs. Add a `maxGenerations` guard:

```typescript
// In MutationAgent.process when action === 'evolve':
if (input.constraints?.maxMutations && lineageDepth >= input.constraints.maxMutations) {
  return currentVariant; // stop growing the tree
}
```

